dsv41 patch 0082 (23.10.2026): DSpark round trace for measurements. Off by default (unset = v24 code path).
Why: the prose campaign needs, per verify round and request, the verify window, the depth the policy chose, the
confidence head's per-position values, the drafts, the target's argmax and p_T of every draft, the kept tokens and the
GPU time of the round. vLLM's counters only give sums; the depth log only histograms.
What: VLLM_DSV41_SPEC_TRACE=<prefix> makes TP rank 0 append JSON lines to <prefix>.rank0.jsonl while the control
file <prefix>.on exists (so one serve can be timed with and without the trace). The hooks read logits, drafts,
confidences and depths; a few extra kernels (top-2, logsumexp, gather on a float copy of the verify rows' logits) and
small copies into pinned host buffers run behind a CUDA event, a writer thread waits for it, so the host never blocks.
Outputs are unchanged with the trace on or off. VLLM_DSV41_SPEC_TRACE_PROMPT=1 adds the prompt token ids per request.
Switches: VLLM_DSV41_SPEC_TRACE (unset/0 = off), VLLM_DSV41_SPEC_TRACE_PROMPT.
